Citation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. iii. 13"},{"id":"7ac077355917","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_heb","w":"chrysostomus.hom_heb","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":34,"p":[22,22],"r":[2,17],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"See 2 Thess. ii. 17. \"Stablish you in every good word and work.\" Probably St. Chrys. had this in his mind."},{"id":"42188c1a5391","v":"npnf.basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","w":"basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":5,"p":[10,10],"r":[1,1],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. i. 1."},{"id":"84b39b480d78","v":"npnf.basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","w":"basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":20,"p":[1,1],"r":[3,5],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"II Thess. iii. 5. A note of the Benedictine Editors on this passage says: \"It must be admitted that these words are not found in the sacred text and are wanting in three manuscripts of this work. Moreover, in the Regius Quintus they are only inserted by a second hand, but since they are shortly afterwards repeated by Basil, as though taken from the sacred context, I am unwilling to delete them, and it is more probable that they were withdrawn from the manuscripts from which they are wanting because they were not found in the apostle, then added, without any reason at all, to the manuscripts in which they occur.\""},{"id":"0cf15785a5fb","v":"npnf.basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","w":"basilius.de_spiritu_sancto","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":28,"p":[1,1],"r":[2,15],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. ii. 15."},{"id":"51c4241e28f8","v":"npnf.basilius.epistulae","w":"basilius.epistulae","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":22,"p":[3,3],"r":[3,10],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Thess. iii. 10."},{"id":"bfac9b9deb86","v":"npnf.basilius.epistulae","w":"basilius.epistulae","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":139,"p":[1,1],"r":[2,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCi